 "notes": "The problematic line reads من در بحر, “from the pearls of the sea.” The three signs of بحر recur independently in عبدكم, وارحموا and الجوهر. The next word starts with three forms for ا ت ن on 96r l.7 before قاكم on l.8 (cf. the opposite middle order ن ت in كنتم). The normal word is انتقاكم, “he chose you”. The first verse gives اتلقاكم and اتوقاكم. In the last verse the wide horizontal double-bar is yāʾ: ا ح ي continues ا ك م on the next line, giving احياكم الرب وابقاكم, “may the Lord give you life and preserve you.” A divider splits ما لي.",
